{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1560048-hera-s-daughters-is-on-the-storypath-nexus","id":1560048,"title":"Hera's Daughters is on the Storypath Nexus!","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2026-05-17T16:35:21-07:00","id":1560048,"title":"Hera's Daughters is on the Storypath Nexus!","content":"I've finally pulled an idea that has been sitting in my brain for four years onto paper. <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/568139/hera-s-daughters?affiliate_id=498510\" target=\"_blank\">Hera's Daughters for Scion 2e is available on the Storypath Nexus</a>!<br /> <br /> <i>When the poets sing of the Olympians, they praise Zeus and Hera\u2019s sons, but forget their daughters. Vicious Ares and ingenious Hephaestus are great Theoi, but their sisters aren\u2019t glorified by poets and historians. Who praises caring Eileithyia, who guides mother and child through birth? Who evokes bloody Enyo, who makes war alongside her brother? Who extols gentle Hebe, cupbearer of Olympus? O great Muses! Lend me your tongue, pen, and genius so we may correct this slight!</i><br /> <br /> <i>This product includes: </i><ul><li><i>Descriptions, Callings, and Purviews for three lesser Theoi: Eileithyia, Enyo, and Hebe. </i></li> <li><i>Eight new Birthrights associated with the Goddesses and their mother.</i></li> <li><i>Four Terra Incognita to expand your story arcs.</i></li> </ul><br /> You can also pick up Hera's Daughters as a bundle with Nile War Gods <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/568141/scion-daughters-go-to-war-bundle?affiliate_id=498510\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> (and get a 15% discount if you already own NWG).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_b